A few years ago, some of us in Florian Jaeger's lab worked through several
chapters of Andrew Gelman and Jennifer Hill's 2007 book, _Data analysis
using regression and multilevel/hierarchical models_.  We all really liked
it (right, guys?).  It's not directed at psycholinguists, but the
exposition is really thorough and clear, and the examples in each chapter
are useful (and worked out in R).  I still refer to it all the time.

The book assumes you already know how to use R, though.  It could serve as
a more technical supplement to the Baayen book, maybe.


